<!--ID=FCB40C2B-1F9F-4C26-B1A1-CF8E67BE07D1;Version=1|{"Files":{}}-->
<!--ID=5B95B1CC-2C7B-494F-B746-CF22A0E779B7;Version=1|{"Locales":{"en-US":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]},"en-GB":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]}}}-->
<speak xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis"
       xmlns:mstts="http://www.w3.org/2001/mstts"
       xmlns:emo="http://www.w3.org/2009/10/emotionml"
       version="1.0"
       xml:lang="en-GB">
  <voice name="en-GB-OllieMultilingualNeural">
    <prosody rate="-10.50%" pitch="-2.50%">
            So the two of them went on until they came to Bethlehem.<break time="500ms"/>
      And when they came to Bethlehem, the whole town was stirred because of them.<break time="500ms"/>
      The women said, is this Naomi?<break time="1000ms"/>
      She said to them, do not call me Naomi, which means pleasant.<break time="500ms"/>
      Call me Mara, which means bitter, for the Almighty has dealt very bitterly with me.<break time="500ms"/>
      I went away full, and the Lord has brought me back empty.<break time="1800ms"/>
      Naomi's grief was honest and open.<break time="500ms"/>
      She did not pretend the loss had not happened.<break time="500ms"/>
      She did not cover her pain with careful words.<break time="500ms"/>
      She simply spoke what was true for her in that moment.<break time="1000ms"/>
      And beside her stood Ruth, who had chosen to share that weight.<break time="1800ms"/>
      They arrived at the beginning of the barley harvest.<break time="500ms"/>
      The fields around Bethlehem were golden and full.<break time="500ms"/>
      The air carried the dry scent of grain waiting to be gathered.<break time="1000ms"/>
      Ruth said to Naomi, let me go to the field and glean among the ears of grain after someone in whose sight I shall find favour.<break time="500ms"/>
      Naomi said, go, my daughter.<break time="1000ms"/>
      So Ruth went out and began to glean in the field behind the reapers.<break time="500ms"/>
      She did not know whose field she had entered.<break time="500ms"/>
      She did not know the name of the man who owned the land.<break time="500ms"/>
      She only knew that she needed to gather enough for the day.<break time="1800ms"/>
      And as it happened, she came to the part of the field belonging to Boaz, who was of the clan of Elimelech.<break time="1000ms"/>
      The text says, as it happened, as though by chance.<break time="500ms"/>
      But in the book of Ruth, nothing is truly by chance.<break time="500ms"/>
      God's provision is woven quietly through every step Ruth takes.<break time="1800ms"/>
      You can rest.<break time="3800ms"/>
    </prosody>
  </voice>
</speak>
